3.0.0 2026-10-30
  - Third public release of 3T MRI data for PAN study. This release covers more subjects than provided by the 3rd PAN Database release.
  - An additional 198 sessions (including 26 longitudinal follow-up sessions) have been added bringing the total number to 1262 sessions (of which there are now a total of 105 longitudinal sessions).
  -  171 new subjects have been added bringing the total number to 1140 subjects.
  - "PhaseEncodingDirection" metadata has been corrected in Baltimore scans. Affected acquisitions are dwi/dwi, fmap/acq-fmri_dir-AP changed from j to j-; and fmap/dir-PA_epi and fmap/acq-fmri_dir-AP changed from j- to j. If these fieldmaps were used for processing the fmri or asl data using sdcflow (e.g. fmriprep, aslprep) then the distortion correction will likely have failed. The diffusion susceptibility distortion correction is however unaffected.
  - The Participants.tsv now has a "baseline_scan_datetime" to help estimate subject age for longitudinal sessions. The age of the participant in the participants.tsv file is the age recorded at the first baseline scan (ses-01) as provided by "baseline_scan_datetime"
2.0.5 2026-10-15
  - "PhaseEncodingDirection" metadata corrected in Baltimore scans. Affected acquisitions are `dwi/dwi`, `fmap/acq-fmri_dir-AP` changed from `j` to `j-`; and `fmap/dir-PA_epi` and `fmap/acq-fmri_dir-AP` changed from `j-` to `j`. If these fieldmaps were used for processing the fmri or asl data using sdcflow (e.g. fmriprep, aslprep) then the distortion correction will likely have failed. The diffusion susceptibility distortion correction is however unaffected.
2.0.4 2026-10-08
  - An additional 2 sessions (including 1 longitudinal follow-up sessions) have been added bringing the total number to 1262 sessions (of which there are now a total of 105 longitudinal sessions).
 - 1 new subject has been added bringing the total number to 1140 subjects.
 - A "baseline_scan_datetime" field has been added to the participants.tsv file to help estimate subject age in longitudinal sessions
2.0.3 2026-10-07
  - The Participants.tsv file has been revised to provide better estimates of participant age as provided at the first baseline scan (ses-01). The difference in years between the subject's registration date in mindcrowd and the date of baseline scan is added to the participant's age recorded at mindcrowd registration. 
2.0.2 2026-10-04
  - An additional 196 sessions (including 25 longitudinal follow-up sessions) have been added bringing the total number to 1260 sessions (of which there are now a total of 104 longitudinal sessions).
  - 170 new subjects have been added bringing the total number to 1139 subjects.
